ment use (ever&#x0002f;never); dietary intakes of fat, fibre, folic acid, total calories (continuous); pack-years of smoking (never&#x0002b;five levels); alcohol intake (continuous); and education (three levels).</p></fn><fn id="t3-fn3"><label>b</label><p><italic>P</italic> for test for interaction between this level of drinking (<italic>vs</italic> never drinking) and heme iron intake&#x0003d;0.69.</p></fn><fn id="t3-fn4"><label>c</label><p><italic>P</italic> for test for interaction between this level of drinking (<italic>vs</italic> never drinking) and heme iron intake&#x0003d;016.</p></fn><fn id="t3-fn5"><label>d</label><p>Restricted to postmenopausal women.</p></fn><fn id="t3-fn6"><label>e</label><p><italic>P</italic> for test for interaction between HRT and heme iron intake&#x0003d;0.49.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>